    "notACompleteRuntimeGraph": true,
    "findings": [
      "Actual new default-off source root composes the existing POST-only native ingress, actual issued intake/official root and a lazily constructed actual scoped durable service session. The old GET application is unchanged.",
      "Actual intake startup loadBound returns an ordinary array, not a frozen array. The new profile requires zero actual BOUND rows before and after SDK initialization; it does not claim recovery or delete historical rows.",
      "Existing POST-v1 client requires 402 Payment Required and 202 BOUND as exact text/plain bodies, and refuses x402 protocol headers on BOUND. The new frame preserves that contract and excludes observer identifiers.",
      "Service admission captures a grant index at session construction. Grant ID may only be available after funding and separate external activation, so opening requires a local explicit late ID rather than a pre-funding ID.",
      "Local admission uses a captured actual ServiceCreditSqliteStore.getGrant method, not an injected store facade or a request-supplied record. The requested ID must match the actual returned record and the retained original transaction, offer, holder, capability, chain and issued digests.",
      "Actual getGrant is a transactional model operation and may persist a lifecycle refresh; calling it is not asserted to be read-only SQL.",
      "Native public close revokes local operator admission before entering the actual native close, retains its exact receipt, independently closes owned funding/service admission once, and never closes borrowed stores.",
      "Actual native response custody in the component was driven only by declared event data. It did not authenticate TLS, sockets, SDK, SQLite, a grant, native closure or production."
    ]
  },
